  "name": "combined_loss_logsigmoid_clamp",
  "intuition": "This crossover combines the core idea of pairwise logsigmoid loss from the first parent with the simpler scaled difference from the second, integrating their best stability features. By using the stable clamp bounds and different scales, it aims to balance the pairwise margin with a direct difference, improving robustness. The combined code merges their structures, ensuring the loss remains numerically stable, passes semantic and dynamic gates, and leverages the best operators from both parents.",
  "pseudocode": "lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n alpha = float(extra.get('alpha', extra.get('hyperparams', {}).get('alpha', 1.0)))\n scale1 = float(extra.get('hyperparams', {}).get('scale1', 1.9496803035382082))\n scale2 = float(extra.get('hyperparams', {}).get('scale2', 0.6752757766189963))\n cost_a = batch['cost_a']\n cost_b = batch['cost_b']\n gap = (cost_b - cost_a).detach()\n x1 = alpha * scale1 * (lpw - lpl) - 0.1 * gap\n x2 = alpha * scale2 * (lpw - lpl)\n x1 = ops.clamp(x1, -20.0, 20.0)\n x2 = ops.clamp(x2, -20.0, 20.0)\n loss1 = -ops.logsigmoid(x1)\n loss2 = -ops.logsigmoid(x2)\n combined_loss = loss1 + loss2\n if weight is not None:\n     combined_loss = combined_loss * weight\n return combined_loss.mean()",
